cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Blind Video Recompression Detection via Bitstream-Level Encoding-Layer Features: A Controlled Protocol and a Negative Result"
abstract: >-
  Artifact for a negative-result study of blind video recompression detection.
  The repository contains a controlled two-arm protocol (single = compress once
  at rate factor q1; double = recompress around q1 with the same codec) that
  removes codec-identity leakage, bitstream-level feature extraction (39
  statistics, no pixel decoding, no GPU), and the evaluation scripts that show
  the bitstream features do not outperform the pixel-domain baseline under
  that protocol.
